<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn Hud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1238">1238</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Hud al-Mutawakkil, al-Mutawakkil ibn Hud</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn Hud, Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Hud al-Mutawakkil, claimed descent from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banu-hud">Hudids</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> and rose against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohads</a> in 1228 in the Ricote valley near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murcia">Murcia</a>. Recognising the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, he briefly united much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> under his rule, but he lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-of-castile">Ferdinand III</a> in 1236 and was murdered in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almeria">Almería</a> in 1238.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibn-hud.jpg" alt="Ibn Hud" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Under the patronage of Alfonso X · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ibn_Hud,_Cantigas_de_Santa_Maria_169.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
